+# Review Draft
+
+## Context
+
+The `Release Smoke Windows ARM` workflow failed in both the GitHub Release archive smoke path and the npm-installed smoke path during version verification.
+
+The binary existed and executed successfully, but `aiwiki-toolkit --version` returns the documented CLI string `ai-wiki-toolkit <version>`. The smoke workflow compared that output to the bare package version, so both paths failed after the executable was already usable.
+
+## What Went Wrong
+
+The workflow duplicated a version expectation instead of reusing the CLI contract that is already covered by `tests/test_cli_version.py`.
+
+## Fix
+
+When a release smoke test runs `aiwiki-toolkit --version`, compare against `ai-wiki-toolkit <package version>` unless the CLI contract itself changes.
+
+For workflow tests, assert the smoke workflow builds that full expected string and does not compare directly against the bare package version.
+
+## Reuse Assessment
+
+This is reusable for release and package-manager smoke tests that validate command-line tools. Thin distribution checks should verify the exact public CLI output, not an inferred subset, otherwise a healthy binary can fail at the final smoke assertion.
